From 170dfc72eb6e448cff6fa96d0c5957eb16b1bd7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:09:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-27: Ctrl+A selects the whole container; undo /
 redo buttons in the title bar (0.27.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Ctrl+A on the design surface (and right-click > 全選): every component in
  the same container as the selection -- an ancestor with an id, the form, or
  a tab sheet (.pcPane has no id, so a tab's components do not drag the other
  tabs' along); the form or nothing selected: the form's own. The selection
  stays the primary when it is one of them (WPF). The menu entry is the sure
  way: VS Code may keep Ctrl+A for itself.
- The designer's title bar gets undo / redo buttons (VS Code's own undo stack
  of the page source), for the mouse.

Tests: probe (Ctrl+A: the button primary, the rest all in its container),
smoke 92 (select all reaches the probe; the buttons run undo / redo), real VS
Code 94 (全選 from the menu: spbSave + sbtExit; the undo button takes an edit
back), lib 120, panels -- all pass; NO-SAVES, MD5-unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
